## What I changed

`scripts/extract_trajectory.py` (one file, surgical):

1. **count_task_reverts** now returns (reverted_sessions, unresolved_tasks, unresolved_sessions) instead of (reverted_tasks, sessions). The two populations are disjoint:
   • `reverted_sessions` — `o["reverted"] is True` (session-level flag, so it sizes a *session* count; the tasks a revert covered aren't in the artifact and are no longer printed)
   • `unresolved_* — lost > 0 with the flag **false**, i.e. NO_VERDICT_NOTE`, the constant Day 209 introduced one function above

2. **render_reverts** prints three named things, reusing NO_VERDICT_NOTE for the third. The unresolved clause only appears when non-zero (planner-prompt context cost).

3. **A real bug fixed along the way: the all-clear keyed on the task count alone, so a session with `reverted: true` and `attempted == succeeded` rendered the clean two-line all-clear and hid a real revert**. Now keyed on all three signals, with a regression row on that exact fixture.

## Evidence

• **Measured population, all 631 outcome.json files on the audit-log branch: `reverted` present in 631, `True` in zero**; 85 sessions have attempted > succeeded, every one flag-false. The word "reverted" was wrong for 100% of the rows that carried it.
• **Live render, same window:** now `0 task reverts in last ~10 sessions. 3 task(s) did not reach a verdict (tree green, no revert recorded) across 3 of the last ~10 sessions.` — previously 3 task(s) reverted across 3 of the last ~10 sessions.
• **Zero path byte-identical** (assert_eq! on the whole string, unchanged text).
• **Absent-key default decided and asserted, not inferred:** absent → not reverted → unresolved, with an anti-vacuous assertion that the fixture really lacks the key.
• **Positive control, one atomic mutate→run→restore (line marked NEUTERED): forcing the flag branch never to fire reddens exactly 5** tests, the discriminating one by name (*"the reverted flag is reported as its own named thing"*) plus the partition row, the all-clear row and the anti-vacuous pair. Restore → ALL PASSED, byte-identical file, 0 markers.
• **Harness: `python3 scripts/extract_trajectory.py --test` → 442 ok, 0 FAIL, `ALL PASSED`. Notably, no CI step invokes --test** (#951), so this run is the only execution those rows will ever get.
• `cargo fmt --check, cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings, cargo build, cargo test` all pass; tree clean.

